# Asymmetric airbrakes with steering: the only scenario that exercises the
# airbrake drag term at all.
#
# `Ship_UpdateAirbrakes` forms
#
#     |airbrake_l - airbrake_r| * Airbrake.drag * |steer| * 0.01 * fs
#
# gated on `fs > 0` (confidence 85, see
# docs/ghidra/functions/psp-pulse/engine.md). Every capture taken before this
# file existed holds both airbrakes at zero for its whole length, so the term is
# **identically zero in all of them** - it has never been observed doing
# anything, in either direction, and a force-balance measurement taken from
# those captures cannot see it. That is why it is explicitly not the along-track
# discrepancy `docs/physics/force-balance-ground-truth.md` measures, and why it
# needs a scenario of its own.
#
# The two halves are mirrored so that the term's *magnitude* can be read
# independently of any sign convention: `|airbrake_l - airbrake_r|` is symmetric
# in the two shoulders, so the left-brake-plus-left-steer half and the
# right-brake-plus-right-steer half must produce the same extra retardation. If
# they do not, the recovered expression is wrong in a way a single-sided capture
# would hide.
#
# The 30-tick straights between the halves are where both brakes are released
# with speed still bled off, which is the only part of the run where the term is
# back at zero at a speed the braked sections also visit - a within-capture
# control.
#
# **This one ends up in a wall too**, and sooner than a plain steering scenario:
# an airbrake on the inside of a turn is exactly how the game is meant to be
# cornered, so the ship rotates much harder than `steer` alone would.
#
#     just trace --port 47810 \
#         --script verification/scenarios/airbrake-asymmetric.inputs \
#         --script-lead 2 --warmup-hold cross --warmup 6 \
#         --out data/traces/talons-junction-airbrake-asymmetric.csv
#
# Reference scenario: Time Trial, Venom, Talon's Junction White, Assegai.

30 cross
50 cross left l
30 cross
50 cross right r
40 cross
